# 01. Purpose

This document answers one question:

> **In what exact order should AEGIS be built so that each stage produces a stable foundation for the next stage without creating architectural confusion or technical debt?**

AEGIS must not be developed by jumping directly from:

```text
Architecture
      ↓
13 screens
```

Instead, development follows:

```text
Architecture
      ↓
Repository Foundation
      ↓
Design System
      ↓
Application Shell
      ↓
Domain Model
      ↓
State Model
      ↓
Data Contracts
      ↓
Service/API Layer
      ↓
Vertical Slice
      ↓
13-Screen Expansion
      ↓
Operational Journey
      ↓
AI Intelligence
      ↓
Security Hardening
      ↓
Observability
      ↓
Testing
      ↓
Deployment
      ↓
Stakeholder Validation
      ↓
Release Candidate
```

---

# 02. The AEGIS Construction Philosophy

AEGIS will be built progressively.

Each phase must produce something that is:

```text
implemented
testable
reviewable
understandable
```

A phase is not complete because files were created.

A phase is complete when its acceptance criteria are satisfied.

---

# 03. Master Build Principle

> **Never build downstream behavior before its upstream contract is stable enough to support it.**

For example:

Do not build complex threat workflows before:

```text
Threat domain model
+
Threat state transitions
+
Threat data contract
```

are defined.

Do not build AI recommendations before:

```text
Threat context
+
Evidence model
+
Decision-support contract
```

exist.

