# 53. Final AEGIS Execution Doctrine

AEGIS will be developed according to these permanent rules:

```text
1. Build foundations before features.

2. Build contracts before integrations.

3. Build one complete vertical slice before expanding horizontally.

4. Build the 13 screens as one system, not 13 independent pages.

5. Keep domain logic outside presentation logic.

6. Keep AI behind explicit service boundaries.

7. Keep humans in control of consequential decisions.

8. Treat mock data as a contract-testing tool, not a replacement for architecture.

9. Test state transitions, not just rendered screens.

10. Test operational journeys, not just individual components.

11. Treat security and auditability as architectural properties.

12. Treat observability as part of the product.

13. Treat stakeholder validation as an engineering requirement.

14. Never allow generated code to silently redefine architecture.

15. Never move forward through an unstable foundation.

16. Every phase ends with evidence.

17. Every major change leaves a record.

18. Every AI agent works inside explicit boundaries.

19. Every implementation must be traceable to a requirement.

20. Every requirement must eventually be traceable to a validated user or system need.
```

